[D,README.md,1] crud-file-server
[D,README.md,2] ================
[A,README.md,1] Basic file server supporting create, read, update, &a delete
[A,README.md,2] 
[A,README.md,3] This package exposes a directory to create, read, update, delete operations.
[A,README.md,4] 
[A,README.md,5] Command-line usage
[A,README.md,6] ==================
[A,README.md,7] 
[A,README.md,8]      crud-file-server [options]
[A,README.md,9] 
[A,README.md,10] This starts a file server server using the specified command-line options.
[A,README.md,11] 
[A,README.md,12] 	-f: file system path to expose over http
[A,README.md,13] 	-p: port to listen on (example, 85)
[A,README.md,14] 	-q: suppress the help message
[A,README.md,15] 
[A,README.md,16] Quickstart
[A,README.md,17] ==========
[A,README.md,18] 
[A,README.md,19]     npm install crud-file-server
[A,README.md,20]     crud-file-server -p 85
[A,README.md,21] 	
[A,README.md,22] Now, navigate to http://localhost:85 and you should see the contents of the current directory as a JSON array.
[A,README.md,23] 
[A,README.md,24] Server-Side Usage
[A,README.md,25] =================
[A,README.md,26] 
[A,README.md,27] 	require('http-proxy').createServer(function (req, res, proxy) {
[A,README.md,28] 		require('subproxy').handleRequest(subProxyHost, port, req, res, proxy);
[A,README.md,29] 	}).listen(port);
[A,README.md,30] 	
[A,README.md,31] Supported operations
[A,README.md,32] ====================
[A,README.md,33] 
[A,README.md,34] **GET** returns a file's contents with the correct mime type, or else the contents of a directory as a JSON array.
[A,README.md,35] **PUT** can be used to write a file.
[A,README.md,36] **DELETE** can be used to delete a file or folder.
[A,README.md,37] **POST** supports two operations, rename and create directory.  
[A,README.md,38] For example, POST http://localhost/newDir?create=directory would create a directory named newDir.  
[A,README.md,39] POST http://localhost/new-directory?create=directory would create a new directory named new-directory.
[A,README.md,40] 
[A,README.md,41] Run the Example
[A,README.md,42] ===============
[A,README.md,43] 
[A,README.md,44] For further clarification, try running the example:
[A,README.md,45] 
[A,README.md,46]     npm install crud-file-server
[A,README.md,47] 
[A,README.md,48] Navigate to the example directory (which should now be under node_modules/crud-file-server/example).
[A,README.md,49] 
[A,README.md,50] 	cd node_modules/crud-file-server/example
[A,README.md,51] 
[A,README.md,52] Run crud-file-server to host this directory. 
[A,README.md,53] 
[A,README.md,54]     crud-file-server -p 3300
[A,README.md,55]     	
[A,README.md,56] Now use your browser to navigate to http://localhost:3300/example.html.  
[A,README.md,57] You will see a simple client that lets you interact with your file system from the web browser.
[A,README.md,58] 
[A,README.md,59] 
[A,README.md,60]     
[A,README.md,61] 
